Z||000016||sjp777||06-25-2001||10:30 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sleeper:<BR><B>translation is something like this:<P>"These photos are of a accident on the expressway in route to Dutra. Não(don't know) confirmed the information of that the speed of the car was 280 Km/h." (i'm guessing)...its not spanish, but it is some form of Latin, anybody know italian or maybe french?<P>what 280km/h to mph.<P>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 06-25-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's neither French nor Italian. It is latin based but not latin itself. Only people who use latin anymore are the clergy and scholars. Pretty much leaves 1 alternative: Portuguese.<P>Lovely pictures. So glad I looked right after I ate.<P>Wheres the other head?<P><BR>Update: It is Portuguese and it says:<P>These photos are of an accident of an entrepreneur on the Dutra Way . It's not confirmed but the information is that it hit the other car at 280 Km/h. <BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg">   <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><P><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
