Z||000020||JSocha||06-26-2001||12:05 AM||||84Bill, I beg you please, do not get me started on a seatbelt war with you regarding higher insurance prices again.  Thought we already hashed that out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000021||JSocha||06-26-2001||12:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>A little off topic, but how do the seatbelts in a Fiero help? I pull on them and they don't hold. Bottom and shoulder straps. Why are they like this?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They are "centrifigal" activated.  Pull slowely, they will not latch, hence the reason you can latch em.  Give em a good fast yank, and they will lock when the centrifical action activates the locking mechanisms.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||sjp777||06-26-2001||12:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B><BR>And sjp777, I am assuming you are a linguistics expert huh?  Quite a useful little talent   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Useful yes, but the $60k I spent on the degree didn't get me a job that pays enough to get ahead on the student loans. I'll be paying them for the next 20 years or so.<P>I knew I should have went for a BS in computer science.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
